{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/128359-some-questions-about-souls-and-interaction-with-mage","id":128359,"title":"Some questions about Souls and interaction with Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-08T10:39:05-07:00","id":128359,"title":"Some questions about Souls and interaction with Mage","content":"I don't play Geist but i ask some questions about souls for Mage the Awakening.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1)What happens to the souls that never produced ghosts ? they will in the Underworld ?<br /> <br /> 2)Ghosts in the Underworld are ghosts who had destroyed all their anchors, but if all (or maybe at least the majority of them) have been &quot;resolved&quot;, they still will in the Underworld ?<br /> <br /> 3)Underworld Ghosts can move on ? is that it is rare and almost all the ghosts who come here are comdaned to stay forever here or it happens very often and the ghosts that remain long are rare and are often not &quot;real ghosts of dead people&quot; ?<br /> <br /> 4)How many are the Ghosts in the Underworld and in the Twillight ? the proportion of underworld ghosts compared to twillight ghosts; and the proportion of deads peoples compared to ghosts of the two categories ?<br /> <br /> 5) What is meta-know in this gameline (outside that think the Sin-Eaters), goes in the direction that ghosts arent souls or not ?<br /> <br /> 6)What think the Sin-Eaters about the Mages ? 6b) and their theory about &quot;ghosts aren't peoples&quot; ? it seems to me a strong area of \u200b\u200bpotential conflict.<br /> <br /> 7)How the Sin-Eaters react to Ghost-Mages ? just &quot;oh, another type of weird ghost&quot; or this is strange even for them and they see that it is different from the rest ? would they be willing to help them as the other ghosts or not ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T11:42:43-07:00","id":128408,"title":"","content":"1) a soul that never produces a ghost is not in any place Sin-Eaters know where they go. Usual afterlife beliefs come along here.<br /> 2) Depends. If the anchors resolution is such that they are able to move on, they do not go to the Underworld. Otherwise they do.<br /> 3) Any ghost can move on. Underworld ghosts are less likley to without outside intervention.<br /> 4) More ghosts are in the Underworld than Twilight, probably, just because most ghosts who do not move on end up there eventually. There is no answer in the setting beyond that to any of this.<br /> 5) I cannot parse this question, can you rephrase?<br /> 6) Most Sin-Eaters assume ghosts are people. Not all of them do. Remember Sin-Eater beliefs vary Krewe by Krewe. People abusing ghosts assuming they are not people can certainly cause conflict, but remember some Sin-Eaters do that. Sin-Eaters do know helping them move on infuses them with plasm and something clearly happens, so more are inclined to belive they are people than not.<br /> 7) Varies Krewe by Krewe, remember beliefs vary by Krewe. They would probably view them as really powerful ghosts, though Sin-Eaters are good at handling even really powerful ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T11:54:07-07:00","id":128423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/128359-some-questions-about-souls-and-interaction-with-mage#post128359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) What is meta-know in this gameline (outside that think the Sin-Eaters), goes in the direction that ghosts arent souls or not ?</div> </div> </div> </div> I spoke to one of the authors who felt that Ghosts are souls; otherwise the game makes no sense.<br /> <br /> (Baron, he was asking &quot;do we know OOC if ghosts are souls or not?&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T12:45:06-07:00","id":128461,"title":"","content":"Ah OK. Then yea, I agree with King's Raven here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T12:50:38-07:00","id":128462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/128359-some-questions-about-souls-and-interaction-with-mage?p=128423#post128423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I spoke to one of the authors who felt that Ghosts are souls; otherwise the game makes no sense.<br /> <br /> (Baron, he was asking &quot;do we know OOC if ghosts are souls or not?&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't try to apply this rule in a mage crossover which has the opposite ruling or the other mage stuff because the nature of both universes are rather closed. It'll vary by which game is the majority and the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:02:10-07:00","id":128467,"title":"","content":"Ghosts aren't souls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:19:34-07:00","id":128470,"title":"","content":"This thread has some useful conversation on many of the same subjects: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/52118-handbook-for-the-recently-deceased\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ently-deceased</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:34:23-07:00","id":128571,"title":"","content":"@Dave<br /> <br /> If ghosts aren't souls then what is that whole passing-on business about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:43:51-07:00","id":128576,"title":"","content":"I think the books have mentioned more than a few times that ghosts aren't souls.<br /> What are they? Ghosts. I don't know beyond that. I have some theories, mainly revolving around them being echoes or memories who for one reason or another aren't accepting their death or aware of it or outright denying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T15:47:33-07:00","id":128580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/128359-some-questions-about-souls-and-interaction-with-mage?p=128571#post128571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Dave<br /> <br /> If ghosts aren't souls then what is that whole passing-on business about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you aware that the latter does not necessarily have anything to do with the former?<br /> <br /> An analogy by way of etymology: the world &quot;resolve&quot; is derived from the Latin word for loosening or unfastening.<br /> <br /> Ghosts' anchors are repeatedly described as things that <i>tie</i> them to the world of mortals.<br /> <br /> Nobody has ever knowingly encountered a ghost again after it has passed on.<br /> <br /> The Great Below's most directly mythological sobriquet, Tartarus, shares phonetics and possibly etymology with a type of accumulated mineral deposit - that is, stuff that has become <i>stuck.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T18:38:18-07:00","id":128679,"title":"","content":"Ghosts not being souls does not necessitate ghosts not <b>having </b>souls. A human being, as a point of comparison, is not a soul. But they possess them. And in the case of someone missing a soul, one cannot just shove a ghost inside them and call it a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T09:02:47-07:00","id":129004,"title":"","content":"I believe the book specifically says that this is one of those vaguely defined things that sin-eaters have different opinions on. I don't see how having or not having them really changes anything either way, except when considering the morality of abusing ghosts I guess. Even that is up to the Krewe to define as part of forming the krewe though, so... meh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T13:26:02-07:00","id":129226,"title":"","content":"I normally interpret ghosts as shed pieces of souls, using the set of Egyptian terms the Mekhet clanbook uses to describe their separated reflections. I see ghosts as <i>influencing </i>the souls they came from, possibly making it healthier for the soul if the ghost is resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T14:16:43-07:00","id":129254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/128359-some-questions-about-souls-and-interaction-with-mage?p=128462#post128462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't try to apply this rule in a mage crossover which has the opposite ruling or the other mage stuff because the nature of both universes are rather closed. It'll vary by which game is the majority and the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>While ghosts are bluebook; I feel that Sin-Eater takes precedence over any other non-bluebook when it comes to ghosts.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, if you have both Mage and Sin-Eater PCs, the Geist books are right about Ghosts. If you have just Mage PCs, than whatever the Mage books say goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/128359-some-questions-about-souls-and-interaction-with-mage?p=128679#post128679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts not being souls does not necessitate ghosts not <b>having </b>souls. A human being, as a point of comparison, is not a soul. But they possess them. And in the case of someone missing a soul, one cannot just shove a ghost inside them and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>This works too.<br /> <br /> (I think it's consistent with what JSnead said too; which was basically - if a Ghost Passing On isn't important to getting them to the proper afterlife then the game doesn't make much sense)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T14:17:21-07:00","id":129255,"title":"","content":"Here's what I've learned on the subject, being particularly interested in this part of the cosmology and watching these discussions for years. I think there's a dissonance between what the readers think of when they use 'soul' and what it means in the gamelines - particularly mage. It's a very fuzzy term to begin with, and probably a poor word to have these discussions with. What we probably should be asking is: are ghosts people?<br /> <br /> The Word of Dave (from the other thread I linked) is that mages are able to sense a... <i>thing</i> inside of humans and it is related to the subtle arcana. They call this a soul. Their magic for severing souls, creating soulstones, etc interacts with this soul thing; they have the ability to sense and manipulate it. The ones that do can say for certain that mages have it, and its brighter/more potent, or something; ghosts do not have it. Also, werewolves do not have it, nor changelings, demons, or a lot of other supernatural things.<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't have souls. Are they still people though - in a respect for life, sentience, or whatever sense of the word?<br /> Ghosts don't have souls. Are they still people?<br /> <br /> The philosophy of Sin-Eaters varies between individuals and krewes, but the base assumption of the game is that most Sin-Eaters still see ghosts as being people, and most believe that what happens to a ghost matters. The how gets a lot fuzzier. But they can't not see and hear ghosts - and ghosts recognize what they are, and pester them a lot; they live their lives with these being. They probably get to know them better than living people, because in a big city, the living can all notice each others and interact, so there's no urgency to do so, but ghosts <i>need </i>things done, and the vast majority of the people they see will never know - the effect is probably like living in a very small town or hobbiest club. All Sin-Eaters eventually see a ghost pass on: they know that when their anchors are resolved, relief and joy fill them up and they drift peacefully into the mysterious beyond; those that are violently destroyed vanish in agony and despair. Most decent human beings would decide at that point that ghosts are still people, and one of these outcomes are better than the other, and that there's probably some kind of cosmic reason that occurs.<br /> <br /> Mages, on the other hand, can cast a spell and say with a certainty that humans have a <i>thing</i> inside them, and ghosts do not; the next logical step is that humans are better than ghosts - at least in a way similar to humans being better than other animals. At that point, it's a lot harder to ignore the political pressures of Necromancers who can do really useful (but morally shady) things with ghosts. Besides, the supernal is the only truth that matters, right? and ghosts have clearly lost their connection to that, so... At best, it's a <i>Mystery</i>. At worst, its justification to use and abuse them however you damn well please.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is a sweeping generalization. Not all mages or sin-eaters will think this way - but enough of them might to perpetuate a stereotype. I see a basic difference in their lifestyles and abilities which lead them to different answers, and which probably propel them into conflict. Sin-Eaters are likely to hate them for slavery and abuse; Mages are likely to be perplexed at why people care so much about what amounts to video tapes.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's the perspective I've come to anyway.<br /> <br /> [TLDR: ghosts aren't souls, but they're probably people - and yeah, mages and sin-eaters would probably start fights over that.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T15:10:29-07:00","id":130295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/128359-some-questions-about-souls-and-interaction-with-mage?p=128679#post128679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts not being souls does not necessitate ghosts not <b>having </b>souls. A human being, as a point of comparison, is not a soul. But they possess them. And in the case of someone missing a soul, one cannot just shove a ghost inside them and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good question is &quot;What <b><i>you</i></b> are ?&quot; <br /> After being dead, you wake up in what ? you are the soul or the ghost ? your consciousness dies with your physical death ?<br /> It's fine &quot;you are made \u200b\u200bup of many things, five if you believes the Mummys, at least your body, your soul and the astral thing that becomes your ghost&quot; but there is an &quot;I&quot;.<br /> <br /> For example, some argue that the entire body is inseparable for your individuality; but you are more your brain than whatsoever else; it is the seat of your consciousness. <br /> If you are anesthetized, after we transplant your brain to a another body; you will wake up in this new body (wich have your brain) and not the former. (although the new biochemistry will have a strong impact over your brain)<br /> <br /> PS: For the example I have excluded the possibility of a soul in real life (for the reason that it is easier to explain and I do not personally believe in the soul), do not be unwelcome if you believe anything else, thank you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}